 "notes": "E265 is the Excavations-sheet row for the same site (distance 0, bearing invalid); its components were coded with grid E265 as the brief asks for other rows. SWP p. 105: the eight tombs lie NW of the tanks (relative_to other); the cisterns lie between the old road and the ruin, and the road's direction is given from et Tell, so no direction from the unit. The Mukam of Sheikh Ahmed is not called a tomb by SWP, so not coded from SWP. Mem III p. 126 (Khurbet Wady Sahyun, 11.9 km, a modern ruined house) is a different place; ignored. Minor OCR noise in SWP text."
